{"name":"Piggyback","hex":"#f0dce3","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"piggyback","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["On somebody's back or shoulders.","Pertaining to transportation of goods where one transportation unit is carried on the back of something else. For example, a truck on a train."]},{"part":"Adverb","definitions":["On somebody's back or shoulders."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/piggyback"}],"entries":[{"title":"Piggyback (transportation)","blocks":[{"text":"Piggyback transportation refers to the transportation of goods where one transportation unit is carried on the back of something else. It is a specialised form of intermodal transportation and combined transport."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bc/Getting_children_out_of_the_fields_and_into_school_%288424375496%29.jpg/330px-Getting_children_out_of_the_fields_and_into_school_%288424375496%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Piggyback_(transportation)","wikidata":"Q2646130"},{"title":"Piggyback (song)","blocks":[{"text":"\"Piggyback\" is a song by American singer-songwriter Melanie Martinez. It was self-released for streaming through her SoundCloud account on December 22, 2017, following a controversy between Martinez and American singer-songwriter Timothy Heller."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/b/b1/Piggyback_Melanie_Martinez.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Piggyback_(song)","wikidata":"Q48815563"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bc/Getting_children_out_of_the_fields_and_into_school_%288424375496%29.jpg/500px-Getting_children_out_of_the_fields_and_into_school_%288424375496%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikip